# ── MARK LV — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials
config/api_keys.json
# the dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/certs/
# a LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your WhatsApp account
config/whatsapp_web/
# Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/token*.json
# Google OAuth client secrets
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*
# Symmetric key for memory encryption-at-rest (core/secrets.py local fallback
# when the OS keychain isn't reachable). Publishing this key defeats the
# entire feature — never commit it.
config/.memory_key

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db
# Short-lived Gemini Live resumption handle (12h TTL by default).
memory/session_handle.json
# One-shot plaintext snapshot kept so a keychain lockout is recoverable.
memory/long_term.plaintext.bak
# SQLite stores that hold private user data (CRM, finance, projects,
# commitments, tasks, vectors, payments, travel). Schema lives in core/*.py;
# data is the user's.
memory/*.sqlite
memory/*.sqlite-wal
memory/*.sqlite-shm

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
